## Appendix C — System-Dynamics Model: Full Specification

### C.1 State Variables

| Variable | Symbol | Units | Initial value |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cumulative launched mass | \( Q(t) \) | kg | \( Q_0 = 5 \times 10^5 \) |
| Marginal transport cost | \( c(t) \) | \$/kg | \( c_0 = 2{,}720 \) |
| Orbital compute capacity | \( K_C(t) \) | MW | 0 |
| Pharma/ZBLAN production | \( K_P(t) \) | kg/yr | 0 |
| Lunar propellant stock | \( K_L(t) \) | kg | 0 |
| Depot utilisation | \( u(t) \) | — | 0 |
| Legal certainty | \( L(t) \) | — | 0.3 |

### C.2 Governing Equations

**Learning curve:**

\[
c(t) = c_0 \left( \frac{Q(t)}{Q_0} \right)^{-\alpha}
\]

**Cumulative mass accumulation:**

\[
\frac{dQ}{dt} = m \cdot \lambda(t)
\]

where \( \lambda(t) \) is launch cadence, driven by demand from the three markets:

\[
\lambda(t) = \lambda_C(K_C) + \lambda_P(K_P) + \lambda_L(K_L)
\]

**Market growth (logistic with threshold-dependent carrying capacity):**

\[
\frac{dK_i}{dt} = r_i \cdot K_i \cdot \left( 1 - \frac{K_i}{K_i^{\max}(c, L)} \right) \cdot \mathbf{1}\{c < c_i^*(L)\}
\]

where the indicator \( \mathbf{1}\{\cdot\} \) enforces the threshold condition.

**Feedback couplings:**

\[
K_C^{\max} = a_C \cdot (c^*/c)^{\eta_C} \cdot (1 + \kappa_{LC} K_L / K_L^{\text{ref}})
\]

\[
K_L^{\max} = a_L \cdot (c^*/c)^{\eta_L} \cdot (1 + \kappa_{CL} K_C / K_C^{\text{ref}})
\]

The parameters \( \kappa_{LC} \) and \( \kappa_{CL} \) are the feedback coupling coefficients, estimated from engineering studies of propellant demand in higher orbits (MEO/GEO/cislunar only; LEO/SSO excluded).

### C.3 Legal Multiplier

\[
\phi(L) = 1 + \pi_0 \cdot \frac{1}{1 + e^{k(L - L^*)}}
\]

with \( \pi_0 = 1.5 \), \( k = 10 \), \( L^* \in [0.4, 0.5] \) treated as an estimand, not a fixed parameter.

### C.4 Numerical Solution

Fourth-order Runge–Kutta, \( \Delta t = 0.01 \) yr, horizon 2026–2040. Monte Carlo: 5,000 draws over \( \alpha \), \( c_0 \), \( r_i \), \( \kappa \)'s, \( L \). Outputs: distribution of \( t^* \) (year of regime transition), distribution of \( S(t) \) at 2040.

