### E.4 Prior and Posterior Computation

Prior \( P(H) \) is computed by ancestral sampling from root nodes through the DAG:

\[
P(H) = \sum_{\text{PT, CR, SHR, RR, CT, SF}} P(H \mid CT, SF) \cdot P(CT \mid \cdot) \cdots P(PT) \cdot P(CR)
\]

With the CPTs above, \( P(H) \approx 0.09 \) (within the 8–12% band asserted in the main text).

When a gate is observed (e.g., PT = Yes), posterior \( P(H \mid PT=Yes) \) is computed via belief propagation. The dissertation reports posteriors for each combination of observed gates.

