Before fitting, the following predictions are registered (OSF timestamped):

| Prediction | Threshold model | Logistic | Power-law |
|---|---|---|---|
| \( d^2S/dt^2 \) sign change | Yes, at \( t^* \) | Yes, one inflection | No (if \( \gamma > 1 \)) |
| Sensitivity to \( c \) | High near \( c^* \) | Low | Low |
| Out-of-sample RMSE on holdout 2026–2030 | Lowest | Middle | Highest |

### F.3 Bayes Factor Computation

Marginal likelihoods computed via bridge sampling. Bayes factor \( BF_{T,L} \) = evidence for threshold over logistic. Decision rule: threshold model supported if \( BF_{T,L} > 10 \) and \( BF_{T,P} > 10 \) on pre-registered holdout.

