## Appendix I — Sensitivity Analysis Plan

### I.1 One-at-a-Time (OAT)

Each parameter varied over its plausible range; output: tornado diagram of \( t^* \) and \( P(S > S^* \mid 2040) \).

### I.2 Global Variance-Based

Sobol indices computed for all parameters, 10,000 Monte Carlo draws. First-order and total-effect indices reported. Priority for empirical estimation assigned to parameters with highest total-effect index.

### I.3 Structural Uncertainty

Three model structures compared: (a) fully endogenous learning, (b) semi-endogenous (learning + exogenous floor), (c) fully exogenous scenario. Results reported for all three; conclusions must hold across at least two.

### I.4 Legal Multiplier Functional Form

Linear, step, and smooth-threshold forms compared. If conclusions are sensitive to functional form, the dissertation reports this as a limitation and uses the range of outcomes across forms as the reported uncertainty.

